Scope

The MIT licence above covers the code in this repository: the analysis and
extraction tools, the x86->C lifter, the recompilation runtime and harness,
the build files, and the documentation.

It does NOT and cannot cover Microsoft Encarta 97 Encyclopedia itself. The
original executables, DLLs, fonts and content files are Microsoft's, are not
distributed here, and you need a legitimate copy of the product to use any of
this. DECO_32.DLL implements a fractal image codec licensed from Iterated
Systems; it is a subject of the reverse engineering here, not a part of it.

A small number of files in this repository are DERIVED from that original
product and are therefore outside the MIT grant as well. They are kept because
the decoders are untestable without them:

  fif_test/*.ftc, *.ftt, *.fif    image fragments extracted from PICON.M20,
                                  used as decoder test vectors
  fif_test/oracle_out/*           execution traces and pixel CRCs produced by
                                  running the original DECO_32.DLL
  encart97.ann                    4-byte annotation stub
  docs/encarta97-running.png      a screenshot of the running program

If you are Microsoft and would like any of that removed, open an issue and it
goes.
